sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — MorphoEval overall 53.0/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "The script is a careful, fully deterministic Python port of the MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust formalism: Fourier-Bessel lateral harmonics with the (-1)^n sign and sin(2n theta0)/(2n theta0) anisotropy factor, Gaussian-difference local harmonics, the second-order perturbative dispersion relation, cubic gamma_3(theta) coefficients and the 2*gamma_3(theta) > gamma_0 roll-stability test all have the published structure, and the PNG, CSV and GIF regenerate byte-for-byte from SHA-pinned fixtures. Its headline \"exact parity to 1e-16\" is parity with another implementation's reported numbers, not with Bressloff et al.; the vendored fixture itself records that the Fig. 40 odd-hex case selects \"honeycomb\" where the paper expects \"triangle\", and the script prints [PASS] for it. The rendered form constants are chosen by preset (pattern, wave_count) rather than by the amplitude equations or the critical wavenumber, the retino-cortical map is the far-field asymptote rather than Eq. 2.1, and the Rule (2011) panel plots upstream Floquet boundaries whose own fit report says calibration_claim_allowed=false. Tunnel and spiral pullbacks look like Klüver/Bressloff figures; the honeycomb is a dot lattice, the GIF's cobweb/honeycomb frames are unrecognisable, and no morphometric is compared against any empirical or literature value. Overall 53.0/100 (faithfulness 44.0, reproducibility 74.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 68c4a1a; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 55, Morphological realism / specimen match 52, Parameter expressivity 35, Morphometric validation 22, Source and data traceability 72, Code-to-model traceability 60, Reproducibility package 85. Output judged: bressloff_v1_form_constants_morphospace.png: rendered output of 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py at 68c4a1a, image/png, 908688 B, 1972×1576 px, artifact_sha256 73edc6aee671456e1d6bdea2581ca8805eabb8aff6b03e95d59ddb3d6ce27514 (sha256 73edc6aee671456e1d6bdea2581ca8805eabb8aff6b03e95d59ddb3d6ce27514), spec_fingerprint fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: fff701034002726a27d7e6e2ee5c626f921c8d06f78514d8965ad139e7a192a7; artifact_sha256: 73edc6aee671456e1d6bdea2581ca8805eabb8aff6b03e95d59ddb3d6ce27514; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/bressloff/driven-neural-fields-registry.json=4f07b5175a48bcb5..., datasets/bressloff/paper-calibration.json=af12b2c1aa3e38fa..., datasets/bressloff/rule-2011-floquet.json=5e349c7b80185de4...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Bressloff et al. (2001, 2002): a Euclidean shift-twist symmetric neural field on the orientation-hypercolumn lattice of V1 undergoes a Turing-type instability whose even (contoured) and odd (non-contoured) planforms, pulled back through the log-polar retino-cortical map, give Klüver's four form constants | Ermentrout & Cowan (1979): cortical rolls map to tunnels, funnels and spirals under the log-polar retino-cortical map | Rule, Stoffregen & Ermentrout (2011): periodic flicker drives 1:1 (stripe) and 2:1 period-doubling (hexagon) Floquet resonance tongues over forcing period and wave number; reconstructed_in_script: Fourier-Bessel lateral coupling, even/odd orientation eigenbranches and marginal-stability scans, cubic amplitude-equation coefficients gamma_0, gamma_3(theta), eta_hex and branch selection, log-polar pullback rendering of four form-constant presets, a Gaussian-only negative control, and an overlay of the Rule (2011) tongue boundaries vendored from the upstream MesmerPrism fixture; transfer_boundary: Numerical parity to ~1e-15 is with the MesmerPrism/bressloff-v1-form-constants Rust implementation's stability_reports, not with digitised figures of the 2001 paper; does_not_claim: Fifth-order resolution of the odd-branch hexagon/triangle degeneracy (Bressloff 2001 Section 5.2), a validated reproduction of Rule (2011) Fig. 8 (the vendored fixture is marked diagnostic-only upstream), or any comparison with psychophysical or anatomical measurements." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants> ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:1123-1171 titles the panel 'Rule et al. (2011) Fig. 8 Floquet Tongues' although datasets/bressloff/rule-2011-floquet.json fit_objective has calibration_claim_allowed=false, acceptance_status='outside-threshold-diagnostic' and note 'not a final published-figure reproduction'; floquet_overlap_rms (0.154) is returned at line 1194 but never printed or drawn. Show the RMS and the upstream status on the panel, and vendor the referenced source-curves file or drop the Fig. 8 claim.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:1227-1230 make_gif overrides every preset to contour_mode='noncontoured', wave_count=3.5, sharpness=1.6; the resulting frames 3/4 and 4/4 (docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif) show four lobes and three blobs that do not resemble a cobweb or honeycomb; animate the same presets as the PNG or raise wave_count to an integer >= 8.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:28 gives Rule 2011 PMID 21980279 while datasets/bressloff/paper_citations.bib:54 gives 21980269, and paper_citations.bib:36 sets year=2001 for Ermentrout & Cowan 1979; line 69 imports scipy.special.iv as bessel_iv but never uses it (the script has its own series at 325-340), making scipy a spurious hard dependency.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:557-587 lattice-local scoping in branch_selection_for makes selected_family a function of the preset's pattern: CSV rows fig38_even_hex_bifurcation and rhombic_stability_angle have identical q*=1.447468, gamma0=0.376848, gamma_hex=0.186897 but report 'hexagonal' vs 'rhombic'. Report global_selected_family (and the stability booleans) in the CSV and figure so selection is a model prediction, not an input.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:638-642 for every non-auto preset wave_number = 2*pi*wave_count/(n*cell_mm), so the rendered cortical wavelength and the k*=12/14/24 'metrics' are preset inputs, not the critical q* from stability_scan; derive wave_number from critical_q/hypercolumn_mm (or document that the render is illustrative).",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:747-761 implements the far-field asymptote r_R=(w0/eps)exp(eps x/alpha) instead of Bressloff 2001 Section 2 / 2002 Eq. 2.1 x=(alpha/eps)ln(1+eps r/w0), y=beta r theta/(w0+eps r), creating an artificial foveal hole r<r_min; and the wavevector's y-component is not quantised to integer cycles over 2*pi*beta/eps (lines 670, 1229 with wave_count=3.5), which produces the visible seam along theta=+-pi in the spiral pullback of the PNG and GIF.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:794-801 and :1004 the azimuthal m4/m6 'lattice discriminator' written to bressloff_v1_metrics.csv is 0.954-0.986 for all four presets including pure rolls, because a single roll has |c_m|=1 for every m; normalise against m2 or use a ratio so the metric actually separates roll/square/hex, and compute it on the retinal pullback too.",
            "remediation needed: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:835-857 verify_paper_calibration_parity compares only to rep['selected_family']/rep['selected_pattern'] (the Rust implementation's actual output) and ignores rep['checks']; datasets/bressloff/paper-calibration.json records for fig40_odd_hex_bifurcation expected 'triangle' vs actual 'honeycomb' with passed=false, yet the self-test prints [PASS]. Surface the upstream checks and fail or flag when the paper expectation is not met.",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:701-706,999-1000,1048 — For non-auto gallery presets (such as fig7_lattice_tunnel and fig31_square_even), render_cortical_and_retinal_planform renders the hardcoded params.pattern ('rings' or 'cobweb') while the retinal subplot title and CSV export report branch_selection['selected_pattern'] ('spiral'), mislabeling cols 1 and 3 of the middle row as mode=spiral.",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:729-742,1227-1230 — Contoured cortical/retinal planforms collapse the orientation dimension via a scalar max-over-orientation tanh envelope rather than rendering Bressloff et al.'s (2001 Figs. 31-36) double-map local orientation contours, and make_gif overrides contour_mode='noncontoured' plus fixed pattern_angle_deg despite a comment claiming a continuous angle sweep.",
            "remediation needed: [second assessor, gemini-4-argon] 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py:793-812,1004 — spectral_ring_metrics computes raw even azimuthal Fourier harmonics (c2, c4, c6) on the cortical grid and exports max(c4, c6) to bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, which evaluates to 0.9862 and 0.9815 for 1D roll gratings (fig7_lattice_tunnel, fig33_rhombic_even_roll) because a 1D stripe grating has all even azimuthal harmonics near 1.0." ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.53"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants faithfully reproduces Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes morphology" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

